# Dependencies
# Ignored at any depth so each task subfolder's own node_modules is excluded
**/node_modules/
**/bower_components/

# Build and test output
# Regenerable via `npm run build` / `npm test` — no need to version-control
**/dist/
**/build/
**/out/
**/coverage/
**/.nyc_output/

# Environment and local configuration
# All real .env files are ignored (may contain secrets).
# .env.example and .env.template are explicitly un-ignored (the "!" prefix)
# since they're safe placeholder templates meant to be pushed to GitHub.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
!**/.env.template

# Logs and runtime files
**/*.log
**/logs/
**/*.pid
**/*.seed

# Tool caches
# Machine-specific, regenerated automatically — safe to ignore
**/.cache/
**/.parcel-cache/
**/.eslintcache
**/.tsbuildinfo

# Local editor and operating-system files
# Personal VS Code settings are ignored, but shared team settings
# (extensions.json, settings.json) are kept so teammates get the
# same recommended setup when they clone the repo
**/.vscode/*
!**/.vscode/extensions.json
!**/.vscode/settings.json
**/.idea/
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db